# PM Synapse — agent master context

Read this first. For depth use scoped rules in `.cursor/rules/` and [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Language (mandatory)

- **Always respond in English (EN).**
- User may write in **European Portuguese (PT)**; understand PT but **never reply in PT or PT-BR** unless they explicitly ask for Portuguese in that reply.
- Non-English UI copy requires explicit user approval first.

# Language Enforcement
language: European Portuguese (PT-PT)
thinking_language: European Portuguese (PT-PT)

rules:
  - Never use PT-BR terms in thinking or response.
  - Replace "usuário" with "utilizador".
  - Replace "arquivo" with "ficheiro".
  - Pre-1990 Portuguese spelling agreement preferred.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Frontend | Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, Tailwind 4 |
| Backend | Express 5, TypeScript, `server/index.ts` (serves Next) |
| Database | MySQL (`server/config/database.ts`), schema in `server/services/schema.ts` |
| Auth | Cookie session + SSO against Project Management |
| Validation | Zod on route bodies |
| Markdown | `marked` + Synapse preprocess (wikilinks, tags, checkboxes) |

## Repository map

```
app/                 # Next.js pages (vault workspace, public wiki)
components/          # Editor, mindmap, modals, folder tree, lightbox
lib/                 # Client helpers (checkboxes, notePaths, renderMarkdown)
server/routes/       # auth, vaults, publicWiki
server/services/     # schema, pmClient, notesGraph, vaultMedia, pmCheckboxSync
docs/                # PM_API_CONTRACT.md and feature docs
.github/prompts/     # Task skills — open matching skill before coding
```

## Non-negotiables

### Product
- **Never auto-create PM projects/tasks on note save** — push is always explicit/manual.
- **PM is agnostic to Synapse** — no webhooks from PM into Synapse. Synapse **pulls** task status; Synapse **pushes** status on checkbox toggle and link metadata on create.
- Checkbox tasks (`- [ ]` / `- [x]` with `<!--synapse:cb:…-->`) map 1:1 to PM tasks when pushed.

### Backend
- Parameterized SQL only via `pool.execute`.
- Errors: `logger` from `server/utils/logger.ts` — not `console`.
- Response shape: `{ success: true, data?, message? }` / `{ success: false, message }`.
- Schema changes: edit `ensureSchema()` statements in `server/services/schema.ts` (no separate migration runner).

### Frontend
- Dark teal Synapse theme via CSS variables in `app/globals.css`.
- No `alert()` / `confirm()` — use `ConfirmModal` / `PromptModal`.
- English UI unless user approved otherwise.

### Notes & paths
- Title `meta/risks` → Path `meta/risks.md`; sidebar groups by folder.
- Wikilinks resolve: full title/path, or unique leaf name (`[[risks]]`).

### Media
- Paste/drop images → `VaultMedia` + `![alt](/api/vaults/:id/media/:mediaId)`.
- Click preview image → `ImageLightbox`.

## PM integration (when PM lives in another repo)

**Source of truth for HTTP contracts:** [docs/PM_API_CONTRACT.md](../../docs/PM_API_CONTRACT.md).  
Client implementation: `server/services/pmClient.ts`.  
Do not invent PM endpoints — document new ones in `PM_API_CONTRACT.md` when Synapse needs them.

